.TH ADICT 1
.SH NAME
adict, aword \- look up words in Acme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adict
[
.B -d
.I dictname
]
[
.I pattern
]
.br
.B aword
[
.I winid
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Adict
runs
.IR dict (7)
in Acme's windows.
With a
.IR pattern ,
a regular expression matched against the headwords as
.I dict
matches them,
it looks the pattern up in
.IR dictname ,
.B pgw
unless
.B -d
says otherwise.
One entry opens a window named
.BI adict/ dictname / pattern
with the entry and the words
.B Prev
and
.BR Next ,
which show the entries before and after it;
more than one opens a window of their headwords, numbered, and button 3 on a number shows that entry.
Button 3 on a word in an entry looks the word up in a new window.
With no
.IR pattern ,
.I adict
opens a window that lists the dictionaries, and button 3 on one opens a window for it.
In a window's name, each byte of the pattern that is not a letter or a digit is
.LR _ ,
and the name keeps the first 20 bytes.
.PP
.I Aword
prints the text of dot in Acme's window
.IR winid ,
.B $winid
by default.
When dot is empty, it prints the word around dot instead: the runes on dot's line that are
neither space nor punctuation, with an apostrophe or a hyphen inside the word kept and one
at its edges taken away, so
.L don't
and
.L well-known
stay whole and
.L ‘well-known’
loses its quotes.
.I Aword
reads the window through its
.BR addr ,
.B ctl
and
.B xdata
files
.RI ( acme (4)).
.PP
In Acme,
.IR hotkey (1)'s
Cmd-K W, in
.BR /lib/hotkey/acme ,
runs
.I adict
on
.IR aword 's
word in the window with the focus,
.BR $acmewin .
It quotes the word's regular expression characters, so dict matches the word literally, and does
nothing for a selection of more than one word or line, one with a
.LR / ,
or a word of more than 64 runes.
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/hotkey/acme
.TP
.B /lib/dict
the dictionaries
.TP
.B /lib/hotkey/acme
Cmd-K W
.SH SOURCE
.B /acme/bin/source/adict
.br
.B /acme/bin/aword
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR dict (7),
.IR acme (1),
.IR hotkey (1)
.SH BUGS
.I Dict
ends a pattern at its first
.LR / ,
so adict cannot look up a word with one.
